# inner_product ci — three dtypes x MB/OC/K scan + tails + degenerate shapes
#
# Shape column = the case's GEMM projection: MxNxK with M = mb, N = oc and
# K = the folded reduction (see tests/inputs/README.md). No params column.
#
# Families covered: the 1x1x1 degenerate form, single-row / single-column
# reductions, ragged mb/oc/k tails, panel-edge K, panel-multiple widths and
# larger reductions.
#
# f32 differential comparison relies on the scalar golden contracting
# `acc += a * b` into an FMA exactly like the vector kernels do; a compiler
# that vectorizes the golden into a non-fused form can land 1 ulp off and
# report a pre-existing f32 failure (same as the matmul and conv2d corpora).
